@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Mixed MVP / future. Retained broader-product associations require explicit future node labels; MVP uses only core/basic ProjectForge.
allowmixing
title MVP + EXPLICIT FUTURE PATHS — Proposed — Persistence responsibilities and authoritative stores
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

component "Resource-owner handler\ncurrent authority / version / invariant" as A
interface "Meaningful owned persistence port" as P
component "Evaluated adapter / ORM mapping" as M
database "Candidate relational primary\nowned records / intent / accounting / references" as D
folder "Private artifacts\nFiles-owned adapter and protection" as F
folder "Native Git objects / refs\nGit-owned semantics" as G
rectangle "Derived cache / projection\nnot authority" as C
cloud "[AFTER MVP] External provider / executor / target\nactual effect truth" as E
A --> P
M ..|> P
M --> D
A --> F : public Files contract
A --> G : public Git contract only
A ..> C : only if selected and correct
A --> E : separate durable attributable effect protocol
note bottom of D
 Replicas, document/search/key-value services and object-store products unselected.
 Local SQL cannot atomically roll back bytes, Git refs or remote effects.
end note

@enduml
